## Why This Is Asked
The scenario mirrors high-throughput services (e.g., payments, telemetry) where multiple producers emit per-topic events and workers must honor per-topic order while applying global backpressure. Designing a two-level queue reveals understanding of memory ordering, contention, and failure modes under load.

## Key Concepts
- Bounded queues and backpressure guarantees
- Per-topic FIFO ordering within a global scheduler
- Lock-free vs fine-grained locking trade-offs
- Memory ordering pitfalls and ABA avoidance
- Testing: burst traffic, latency, starvation, failure modes

## Code Example
